            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0177" n="1011" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1011"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/692</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1918-11-14T19:48:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1918-11-11T00:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 14, 1918, 7.48 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3734. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 1872. Your 1207, Department’s 2661, November 6, 7 p.m. In accordance with
                    your approval of joint certification plan, Foreign Office will telegraph
                    following instructions to British consuls at Buenos Aires, Montevideo, Bahia,
                    Santos, and Rio de Janeiro, under date of November 18.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>In order to facilitate clearance of vessels calling for bunkers at U.S.A.
                        ports on their way to Scandinavia and Holland, arrangements have been made
                        with the W[ar] T[rade] B[oard] at Washington that particulars of proposed
                        cargo should be communicated to their United States colleagues by British
                        consul, and Foreign Office notification of cargo approved by the Allied
                        Blockade Committee, at present telegraphed to them, to United States
                        colleagues in order that the manifests may receive joint certification by
                        representatives of both Governments. You should make arrangements with local
                        shipping agents and communicate with your United States colleagues
                        accordingly, similar instructions being sent by the United States
                        Government.</p>
                </quote>
                <pb facs="0178" n="1012" xml:id="pg1012"/>
                <p>Will you have State Department telegraph instructions in the same sense to
                    American consuls at above ports effective November 18?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
